    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 2 part 4a P1 run.log (specs/0019-names-links-properties-
    # protection.md, "P1: defined names, creating an element in the workbook"
    # and "Harness runs", `--names-sample` and P1, with "Planning rulings during
    # P1"):
    #   1. the release binaries built at the phase commit on both targets and
    #      hashed;
    #   2. the corpus run with --tool-arg --names-sample on both targets,
    #      recorded as m2p4a-p1-<utc-date>-<shortsha>.md and .txt, the record
    #      checked against the run directory table by table;
    #   3. the run log's own comparison (namescmp.py, python3, zipfile, byte
    #      spans and ElementTree, printed below) over every output of both
    #      labels: the workbook part outside definedNames and calcPr
    #      byte-identical; the input's definedName elements a byte-identical
    #      prefix of the output's; the two added elements' start tags built here
    #      (the localSheetId W's index), their texts' lengths, and their bytes;
    #      a created container in schema position (the log's own copy of the 19
    #      names); calcPr with fullCalcOnLoad set, or created in schema
    #      position; the root children's order; one of each; the names read
    #      back; each tool line's counts against the comparison's; a planted
    #      control per flag on the first workbook in manifest order where it
    #      applies; the two labels' outputs byte for byte;
    #   4. the keep regenerated on both targets, compared, and against part 3
    #      P4's committed open-check record; the edit open check over the host
    #      keep, recorded as m2p4a-open-<utc-date>-<shortsha>;
    #   5. this script's own standard error counted (specs/0017 P1 verification
    #      ruling 7).
    # No name, text, sheet name, reference, target, value or part name from the
    # corpus is printed.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4a P1 from part 3 P1's run script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p3-p1/run.log; its change list F to J is there), the last
    # run script that built its own release binaries and ran one sample, with
    # the rules part 3 P2 to P4 added (printed in records/logs/m2p3-p4/run.log,
    # changes X to AD). What differs, and why:
    #  AE. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4a-p1/scripts, on the disk,
    #      not a tmpfs scratchpad: specs/0018 close-out ruling 4, a superseded
    #      attempt stays on disk under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4a-p1/), the
    #      build directory (m2p4a-p1/run) and the keep (m2p4a-p1/keep-host) are
    #      this phase's; the base is part 3's close-out record commit ("M2 part
    #      3 close-out record:"); the phase commit is P1's tool commit by its
    #      subject; the record stems are m2p4a-p1- and m2p4a-open-.
    #  AF. fmtcmp.py is replaced by namescmp.py, written for this phase; the
    #      checks, the line's keys and the entry expectation are
    #      --names-sample's: the workbook part changed in every workbook; with a
    #      calculation chain, the chain entry dropped and the workbook's rels
    #      part changed, and [Content_Types].xml changed when it holds an
    #      Override for the chain (--formula-sample's expectation, specs/0019
    #      "Harness runs"); every other entry identical.
    #  AG. The record check's family expectations follow AF: the changed
    #      entries' families are workbook, and rels and content-types where a
    #      chain was dropped; the dropped entries' family is calcChain alone; no
    #      entry is added.
    #  AH. The keep is compared with part 3 P4's committed open-check record
    #      (records/m2p3-open-2026-09-27-b728fdf, added by "M2 part 3 P4
    #      record:").
    #  AI. Change AB of part 3 P4 is carried: keep_pairs_ok and run_listing_ok
    #      run every time over a planted keep listing and a planted run
    #      directory, each with a control that must fail; a moved run directory
    #      is listed by run_listing and hashed.
    #  AJ. Every log pins the spec's hash (specs/0018 close-out ruling 4): the
    #      spec check accepts only the uncommitted copy at SPEC_SHA or the
    #      committed file, and prints both hashes.
    #  AK. The records' destination is a parameter, RECORDS_DEST (default
    #      records, the repository's), so a dry run never writes into the
    #      repository; the logged run leaves it unset.
    #  AL. This phase's test.log prints the keep-variable line without part
    #      3's "(header change 6)" label, so tl_unset reads that form.
    #  AM. Attempt 2: AE's comment spelled a placeholder-shaped path no root
    #      line declares, which the scan pre-check's placeholder check found in
    #      attempt 1's printed script (the carried rule of specs/0017 close-out
    #      ruling 4); the comment now names the phase's directory. The run takes
    #      RUN_SUFFIX -b, and names attempt 1's run directory and keep for moving.
    #  AN. Attempt 3: test.log was rerun after independent check 1 (its F5, the
    #      plants' assertion output), and this log reads and hashes test.log, so
